-- Mindfries — seed the Targets panel with the hand-picked company list.
--
-- 102 companies. Run AFTER the three migrations (target_companies
-- must exist). Safe to re-run: 'on conflict (company_key) do nothing' leaves a
-- company already in the table exactly as it is, edits and all.
--
-- company_key is computed here with the app's own companyKey() rule
-- (lower-cased, punctuation to spaces, legal suffixes dropped) so the unique
-- constraint and the app's duplicate check agree. Don't hand-write it.
--
-- owner is left null: nobody has been assigned these yet, and the panel shows
-- "unassigned" honestly rather than guessing. next_action_due is null too, so
-- nothing shows as overdue on day one.

on conflict (company_key) do nothing;

-- How many landed:
select count(*) as targets from target_companies;

-- ── Held back ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- "AssemblyAI Canada" is the same company as "AssemblyAI" (both assemblyai.com). The unique
-- constraint wouldn't catch it, because the keys differ, but the panel's own
-- Add form matches on website host and would refuse it as a duplicate.
--
-- Uncomment only if it really is a separate entity worth tracking on its own:
--
-- insert into target_companies
--   (name, company_key, website, priority, stage, why_target, notes, source, next_action)
-- values
-- ('AssemblyAI Canada', 'assemblyai canada', 'https://www.assemblyai.com/', 'A', 'researching', 'AI model/API company with engineering and ML hiring', '51-200 employee profile; actively hiring; Canada-linked presence.', 'tracker', 'Find founder/CTO/Head of Talent; identify one active role and send a role-specific Mindfries pitch')
-- on conflict (company_key) do nothing;
